CORE
temporal_assumption1.sv
--bdd
^\[main\.assume\.1\] always \(main\.a \|=> main\.b\): UNSUPPORTED: assumption not supported by BDD engine$
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r -> main\.b: INCONCLUSIVE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The BDD engine can only add assumptions of the form "always p" with a
state predicate p to the transition relation.  An assumption with a
temporal operator is unsupported and must not be silently ignored, as
this is unsound: the property holds under the assumption, but would be
reported as REFUTED without it.  The assumption is therefore marked
UNSUPPORTED, and the dependent property INCONCLUSIVE.
